Ladybird now skips computing a flex item’s automatic minimum size only
where its specified size suggestion is at most its flex base size:
That’s the condition under which Blink’s FlexLayoutAlgorithm::
ConstructAndAppendFlexItems() skips it too. Gecko decides it per item
from the min-size alone, in FlexItem::IsMinSizeAutoResolutionNeeded(),
and WebKit computes it whenever min-size is auto. In Chrome 158, Firefox
151 and WebKit 26.5 (engine-compare), the reduction’s items get the
sizes Ladybird now gives them: 100px where the flex-basis is 0px or 50px
and the width is 100px, their 300px content where the width is 400px,
and a height of 100px in a column container.
